    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d411-a2">

                <pb facs="0580" n="266" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg266"/>


                <p rendition="#flush">Foreign Office, No. 111a.19785/02997</p>
                <p rendition="#center">NOTE VERBALE</p>
                <p>In supplement to its notes verbales of August 6, 1914, and October 22, 1914,
                    IIIa.9222 and 17064, the Foreign Office has the honor to inform the Embassy of
                    the United States of America that during the present hostilities the following
                    will be considered by Germany as conditional contraband in addition to the
                    articles and materials designated under 11, 1-16:</p>
                <p>17. Woods of all kinds, rough or worked (in particular hewn, sawed, planed,
                    grooved), charcoal cylinder tar.</p>
                <p>18. Sulphur, crude or refined, sulphuric acid.</p>
                <p>The Foreign Office begs that the Embassy will kindly notify its Government of the
                    above as soon as possible.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1914-11-23">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 23, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
